<body>
<h1>HA Decision: &lt;service-name&gt;</h1>
<h2>Context</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Service:</strong> &lt;service-name&gt;</li><li><strong>SLA target:</strong> 99.99% (~52 min/year)</li><li><strong>Customer geography:</strong> US + EU</li><li><strong>Current state:</strong> {{ describe }}</li></ul>
<h2>Decision</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Choice</th><th>Rationale</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>LB instances</td><td>2 (managed ALB in each region)</td><td>rule two-lb-min</td></tr><tr><td>AZs used per region</td><td>3</td><td>rule two-az-min</td></tr><tr><td>Backends per AZ</td><td>2</td><td>rule two-az-min</td></tr><tr><td>GSLB</td><td>AWS Global Accelerator (anycast)</td><td>rule anycast-over-dns-for-9999</td></tr><tr><td>Drain on SIGTERM</td><td>yes, deregistration_delay = 30 s</td><td>rule drain-on-sigterm</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Failure-domain analysis</h2>
<table><thead><tr><th>Failure</th><th>Blast radius</th><th>Mitigation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Process crash</td><td>1 instance</td><td>managed LB removes via health-check</td></tr><tr><td>Host failure</td><td>1 instance</td><td>AZ-level spread absorbs</td></tr><tr><td>AZ failure</td><td>1/3 of one region</td><td>2 AZ remain with capacity</td></tr><tr><td>Region failure</td><td>1 region</td><td>Global Accelerator fails over to peer region</td></tr><tr><td>BGP route flap</td><td>edge PoP</td><td>client retry; anycast reroutes within ~30 s</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2>Operational requirements</h2>
<ul><li>Chaos drill: monthly LB-instance kill + quarterly region failover.</li><li>SIGTERM handler: see sigterm-drain.py (sigterm-drain.py).</li><li>Alert on healthy-target-count &lt; 2 in any AZ.</li></ul>
<h2>Status</h2>
<ul><li>[ ] Approved</li><li>[ ] Deployed</li><li>[ ] Drill passed</li></ul>
</body></html>
